IMPORT prelude

-- Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994 (Qld) -- small date and amount helpers for mai-core.l4 and mai-seat.l4. Built on
-- the stable prelude's date primitives (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR);
-- the daydate library is not imported, and no YMD is defined.
--
-- READINGS (the Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld) is not deposited, so these are the encoder's):
-- * "within 1 month after" a day ends on the same day of the next month; "within 3 months", "6 months", "9 months"
--   the same way. The day of the event is excluded and the corresponding day is the last day.
-- * A period of months that starts on a day the end month does not have (31 May + 1 month) ends on the last day of
--   the end month (30 June).
-- * "within 14 days after" a day ends 14 days later; "within 60 days after" ends 60 days later.
-- * "at least 7 days before" a day ends 7 days before it.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates and amounts`

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
      `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` `x` `and` `y` MEANS
    IF `x` AT MOST `y` THEN `x` ELSE `y`

GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` `y` IF
        (`y` MODULO 4 EQUALS 0 AND (NOT (`y` MODULO 100 EQUALS 0)))
    OR  `y` MODULO 400 EQUALS 0

GIVEN `m` IS A NUMBER
      `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` `m` `of` `y` MEANS
    IF `m` EQUALS 2
    THEN IF `is a leap year` `y` THEN 29 ELSE 28
    ELSE IF `m` EQUALS 4 OR `m` EQUALS 6 OR `m` EQUALS 9 OR `m` EQUALS 11
         THEN 30
         ELSE 31

-- The same day n months later, or the last day of that month where it is shorter.
GIVEN `n`         IS A NUMBER
      `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `n` `months after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (`the smaller of` (DATE_DAY `the start`) `and` (`the days in month` `end month` `of` `end year`)) `end month` `end year`
    WHERE
        `months counted from year 0` MEANS ((DATE_YEAR `the start`) TIMES 12) PLUS ((DATE_MONTH `the start`) MINUS 1) PLUS `n`
        `end year`  MEANS TRUNC (`months counted from year 0` DIVIDED BY 12) 0
        `end month` MEANS `months counted from year 0` MINUS (`end year` TIMES 12) PLUS 1

GIVEN `n`         IS A NUMBER
      `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `n` `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL ((DATE_SERIAL `the start`) PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `n`         IS A NUMBER
      `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `n` `days before` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL ((DATE_SERIAL `the start`) MINUS `n`)

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE
      `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a` `is no later than` `b` IF DATE_SERIAL `a` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE
      `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a` `is after` `b` IF DATE_SERIAL `a` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE
      `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `a` `to` `b` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `b` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `a`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE
      `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` `a` `and` `b` MEANS
    IF `a` `is no later than` `b` THEN `b` ELSE `a`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE
      `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of` `a` `and` `b` MEANS
    IF `a` `is no later than` `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- A percentage given as a number (25 for 25%) taken off an amount.
GIVEN `amount`  IS A NUMBER
      `percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reduce` `amount` `by percent` `percent` MEANS
    `amount` TIMES ((100 MINUS `percent`) DIVIDED BY 100)
